# KaiOS app (`src/app/`)

- Every file in `src/app/js/` is an IIFE that attaches its public surface to `window.App` (`App.store`, `App.screens.chat`, ...). `js/core/bootstrap.js` creates `window.App`.
- Scripts load in the order listed in `src/app/index.html`; a new module needs a `<script>` tag there, after the modules it uses at load time.
- Folders: `core/` (platform, util, config, http, db), `data/` (api, normalize, ws, store, wake), `ui/` (widgets), `screens/` (one screen per file, `App.screens.<name>.create(...)`).
- Target Gecko 84 and 123 (ES2020). Match the surrounding ES5 style (`var`, `function`, `['catch']`).
- Build DOM with `App.util.el(tag, className, text)`; never use `innerHTML` with untrusted content.
- Log with `App.util.dbg(msg, data)` (Settings → Debug log). Use `App.toast(msg)` for transient notices and `App.notice` for persistent ones.
- Reach KaiOS B2G APIs (activities, alarms, device storage) only through `App.platform`.
- Talk to Signal through `App.api` → `App.signal`; HTTP goes through `App.http` (mozSystem XHR).
- `ws.js` ACKs an envelope only after decrypt and persistence succeed; keep it that way.

```js
// Good
row.appendChild(App.util.el('span', 'hint', contact.name));
// Bad: untrusted text as HTML
row.innerHTML = '<span class="hint">' + contact.name + '</span>';
```

- The privileged CSP forbids inline handlers, inline `<script>`/`<style>`, `eval`, and `new Function`; `scripts/package.sh` fails the build on `eval(`.
- `src/app/vendor/*.bundle.js` and `*.wasm` are build output; edit `src/engine/` or `src/native/` instead.
